  "id": "chirimia_chocoana",
  "name": "Chirimía chocoana (Quibdó street band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The chirimía of Chocó is the Afro-Colombian wind-and-drum band of the Atrato river towns, above all Quibdó, where it leads the processions and street dancing of the Fiestas de San Pacho for Saint Francis of Assisi, inscribed by UNESCO in 2012. A typical band has clarinets, a bombardino (euphonium), redoblante (snare drum), tambora (bass drum) and platillos (cymbals), playing abozao, jota chocoana, porro and polka. The baritone-horn card stands in for the bombardino, the snare-drum card for the redoblante and the bass-drum card for the tambora.",
  "recipe": "classic early-2010s chirimía chocoana, carnival Processional. clarinet, baritone horn bb, snare bass drum, credited cymbals. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
